-
-Keep the main PRD usable as an entry point with all 13 required headings in order. Put complete local detail and acceptance material in canonical supporting files when useful; provide task-specific reading routes rather than requiring every slice to reread every section or fixture. Keep shared orientation limited to the outcome, protected constraints, major responsibilities, shared decisions, canonical locations, dependencies, and integrated results. Each shared rule belongs with the smallest scope capable of owning it, not an ever-growing root document or competing local copies.
-
-Within delegated authority, divide detailed work and implementation into smaller coherent assignments. Every split preserves parent obligations, fixed decisions, shared contracts, authority, acceptance contributions, and any open gate. Allocate each inherited duty to a child contribution or an explicit retained shared responsibility; assign new integration and verification work. A split cannot turn recovery, a spanning invariant, or a parent blocker into a non-goal. Keep delivery tied to integrated capabilities rather than territory-by-territory completion.
